ors a behaviour that demonstrably exists, including the sibling-preserving placement.","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p8","ref":"t5 PICKER PARTITION (c35)","kind":"inventory","severity":"LOW","premise":"THREE distinct daemon companion renderers (ER, sequence, component) all stamp the SAME companion kind `diagram-mermaid` in src/workflow/artifacts/companion/render.ts — which is why a companion ref cannot identify its own source record, and why t5's uxPickRef must be proved to PARTITION the companions array against S003's dgPickRef rather than merely match.","evidence":"All three reads resolve verbatim: `src/workflow/artifacts/companion/render.ts:104`, `:205` and `:243` each read `kind:    'diagram-mermaid',`. The claim is independently corroborated in src by `src/workflow/artifact-content.ts:67` ('THREE daemon renderers stamp kind:'diagram-mermaid' (companion/render.ts:104...') and by the committed test comment at `src/workflow/__tests__/artifact-content.test.ts:332`.","action":"none — verified sound. A companion ref genuinely cannot identify its own source record, which is what makes t5's picker-partition check necessary rather than pedantic.","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p9","ref":"t5, t6","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A companion kind DISTINCT from the three diagram kinds identifies the experience mock in the daemon's companion vocabulary — without such a distinguishing kind, t5's picker-partition acceptance check is unsatisfiable and the ux slot could not be told apart from a diagram slot.","evidence":"`src/workflow/artifacts/companion/types.ts:24` reads `export type CompanionKind = 'diagram-mermaid' | 'diagram-html' | 'ux-mock';` — a closed three-member union in which `ux-mock` IS distinct from both diagram kinds. Producers stamping it are confirmed across 14 src/ matches of `kind: 'ux`, and the plugin side already maps the union totally (`docs-review-panel.test.ts:2346`: 'companionVisualKind maps the closed union TOTALLY — both diagram