cross the four ledger records, so 23 and 41 are unconfirmed by this evidence.","action":"Re-derive both counts over the four ledger records before leaning on them in t2's rationale. The materiality is limited and that is why this is MED, not HIGH: the acceptance check PRESCRIBES mapping every TextBlock modifier to the daemon's class, and ux.ts:356 confirms the daemon does exactly that for isSubtle — so the mapping obligation is correct regardless of whether the occurrence counts are 23/41 or some other pair. Only the strength of the 'would flatten the authored emphasis' argument depends on the numbers.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The counts are rhetorical support for an obligation that is independently grounded in the daemon's own mapping at ux.ts:356. Re-derive them so the figures in the artifact are real; do not change the acceptance check."}},{"claimId":"p13","ref":"t2 (c6)","kind":"inventory","severity":"LOW","premise":"The docs-review webview currently carries exactly FOUR inlined source strings of the DOCS_*_SOURCE family (DOCS_BODY_RENDERER_SOURCE, DOCS_SECTIONS_SOURCE, DOCS_FR_SOURCE, DOCS_DIAGRAM_SOURCE) concatenated into ONE nonce'd script — so DOCS_UX_SOURCE is the FIFTH, and the committed parse-coexistence guard must be extended from four to five. NOTE: this file lives under vscode-plugin/, not src/, so a src-scoped grep cannot re-derive it.","evidence":"All four reads resolve verbatim to declarations in ONE file: `vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts:76` `export const DOCS_BODY_RENDERER_SOURCE =`, :111 `export const DOCS_SECTIONS_SOURCE =`, :185 `export const DOCS_FR_SOURCE =`, :369 `export const DOCS_DIAGRAM_SOURCE =`. The `const DOCS_[A-Z_]+_SOURCE` pattern yields exactly FOUR declarations in the plugin tree, so DOCS_UX_SOURCE is genuinely the fifth and the parse-coexistence guard must move from four to five.","action":"none — verified sound. The 'fifth member' framing and the guard extension are both correct.","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p14","ref":"t2 injection-site count","kind":"inventory","severity":"MED","premise":"The emitted docs-review shell contains EXACTLY ONE markup-injection site today — the guarded vendored markdown body parse — and t2's acceptance check requires that count stay at one after a fifth source string joins. NOTE: vscode-plugin/, not src/.","evidence":"The injection-site COUNT is not re-derived: `\\.innerHTML\\s*=` returned 50 matches and every surfaced one is from docs/ (the cap was exhausted by prose), so the evidence cannot establish that the emitted shell has exactly one. What the evidence DOES confirm is the adjacent ban: three committed plugin tests assert the other sinks are absent — `docs-review-panel.test.ts:755` (`assert.doesNotMatch(html, /insertAdjacentHTML|outerHTML|document\\.write/`), :1227 and :2748 (iterating a banned list including innerHTML).","action":"At t2, assert the COUNT and not merely the ban — count `.innerHTML=` occurrences in the emitted shell and assert the total is 1, identifying it as the guarded body parse. A ban on the other three sinks passes even if a second innerHTML assignment is added, which is precisely the gap this premise is supposed to close.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The existing committed tests ban sibling sinks but the evidence does not show the one-site count being pinned. t2 already states the count obligation; the fix is to make sure the test counts rather than bans."}},{"claimId":"p15","ref":"t1 (c1, c3)","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"The uxDefinition record already reaches the extension host on DocsContent (declared at docs-review-client.ts:37, forwarded at :113) and is DROPPED before the webview message is posted — so t1 is genuinely a one-hop forwarding change and not a new data path. NOTE: vscode-plugin/, not src/.","evidence":"Both reads resolve EXACTLY and this is the Story's central premise. `vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-client.ts:37` reads `re